From: Leo <62428370+LeoooChen@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] firewall4: resolve VLAN lower devices from the netifd class

netifd reports its device class as type (VLAN, 8021q, 8021ad or bridge).
The optional sysfs devtype is absent for some VLAN interfaces, so fall
back to the netifd class while retaining the existing devtype behavior.

Signed-off-by: Leo <62428370+LeoooChen@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/root/usr/share/ucode/fw4.uc
+++ b/root/usr/share/ucode/fw4.uc
@@ -428,8 +428,10 @@ function resolve_lower_devices(devstatus, devname) {
 	let devs = [];
 
 	if (dir) {
-		switch (devstatus[devname]?.devtype) {
+		switch (lc(devstatus[devname]?.devtype ?? devstatus[devname]?.type)) {
 		case 'vlan':
+		case '8021q':
+		case '8021ad':
 		case 'bridge':
 			let e;
 
